{"title":"2025 SSMO Tiebreaker Round Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Case_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Case_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Case_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Case_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Case 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Summing_Up\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Summing Up</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a2706d93bec82f27659723491262794282f870be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8\\} \\to \\{1, 2, 3, 4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"282\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed95d99e1e5316fac0a49b90e13c98ac0dd86941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2f(x)) = f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c92fc7dcbfb32018e54c66cca50640743a5134a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028d59f5f255262894b49646f92f67941d202454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. Then, we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/b/66bba56e3aa3287297a232db0587b5d390997058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2y)=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />. We can see that if there exists a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/b/febb3ae7e845f29c597761dccb9307a114bc5678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j\\in \\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd537f49d441c887a8779cd089e07648107a213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(j)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/2/7b23f1349494376ceaaf1dace87da885c81a68d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26f8e7710691ace81b6870d231f5d558879ad65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(j)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a994ec488d8823266577f2242ec10c11113e0c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(4)=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/8/f8812310d0f197830895a0d346d46f0103586433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(j)=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c9b6237d4dd44c09d535be3d805a6f5f8d3c66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(6)=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90fb592dbeeb73ec9f1b04bf50cefe95c27dca07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(j)=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f7ade8a11ec37d0cc5a5bc4bcf51715beaa49d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(8)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. Now let's do some cases.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_1\">Case 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Case 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let's say that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> number from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed123aec81a19e7c53d2af259f3b30d52b9b6d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> can be gotten. That number has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices. All of our numbers in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79f4d83d3eee9fa9f12d3dcff13b626872c4c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> then must be that one possible result, so this case produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mappings.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_2\">Case 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Case 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let's say that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed123aec81a19e7c53d2af259f3b30d52b9b6d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> can be gotten. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29cc82febefd93ffd2d53ed68a4eb8376c2ce9a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom42=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose these numbers. We now must have exactly two numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119358660d837ad98b58a5820e60e7e34df8bc12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,4,6,8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> to have a fixed value after being inputted into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. That means we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that can be any of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values, so this will produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/3/713053eba09421fb5dba1dc708b930ab6a10ae58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\times2^6=384$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> mappings.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_3\">Case 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Case 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let's say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed123aec81a19e7c53d2af259f3b30d52b9b6d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> can be gotten. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/8385bb45335612d73c8e4a68f6426bdc79fea85d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom43=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" /> ways to choose these numbers. We now must have exactly three numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119358660d837ad98b58a5820e60e7e34df8bc12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,4,6,8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> to have a fixed value after being inputted into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. That means we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that can be any of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values, so this will produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10e3b8efc849fe6375d5249a00d4adda229fe44f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\times3^5=972$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> mappings.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Case_4\">Case 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Case 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let's say that all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed123aec81a19e7c53d2af259f3b30d52b9b6d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> can be gotten. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08345e956445c7b30acc23559be2199ada32c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom44=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" /> ways to choose these numbers. We now must have all the numbers from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/9/119358660d837ad98b58a5820e60e7e34df8bc12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,4,6,8\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> to have a fixed value after being inputted into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />. That means we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that can be any of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values, so this will produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec1bea6e2eb8b71edbf4c00a06e7b29bbdc0bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\times4^4=256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" /> mappings.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Summing_Up\">Summing Up</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_SSMO_Tiebreaker_Round_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Summing Up\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Summing up the cases, we have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/095de20a987bb5b9705de5136c8f1e11aa474936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+384+972+256=\\boxed{1616}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"231\" height=\"25\" /> possible mappings. \n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033045\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 238/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7894/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33828:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018033045 and revision id 287035. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}